  "sport": "floorball",
  "title": "Dubbeldonken – the double M with two passes",
  "description": "The same set-up as Donken (the M): two lines, one in each corner beside the goal, and a cone on each side further out. Here every player has three jobs on their side: pass from the corner, receive halfway and pass on, and finally run round the cone and shoot.\n\nThe first player in the left line runs down and round the cone. The next in the left line passes across to the right-hand player, who has run halfway down. They play a diagonal pass to the runner at the cone, who turns and shoots first time. Then the right-hand player carries on round their cone and gets the pass from the left player, who is now halfway – and it keeps rolling both ways. After the shot, the shooter joins the other line. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Passes along the floor, to the blade."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "The halfway player receives with the body turned towards the cone and moves the ball on quickly."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "The runner turns sharply round the cone and shows with the stick where they want the ball."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Shoot first time – do not stop the ball first."
    }
  ],
